{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=3c4d4b7b-1f58-8bea-9fd3-8ca0e41684ff": {
      "title": "Title IX Specialist",
      "description": "Title IX Specialist - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings Title IX Specialist Department: Office of the President Location: Chicago, IL START YOUR APPLICATION Title IX Specialist Compensation: $48,000 - $50,000, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Position Type/Schedule: This is a Full-Time, exempt position, Monday through Friday, 8:30 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Work Location: Illinois Tech, 10 West 35th Street, Chicago, IL 60616. Work Authorization: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States, both presently and for the duration of employment with the university General Description The Title IX Specialist is responsible for helping to support the university’s compliance with the requirements set forth by the Title IX Educational Amendments Act, the Clery Act, the Violence Against Women Act (VAWA), and the Illinois Preventing Sexual Violence in Higher Education Act. The Title IX Specialist will report to the Title IX Coordinator and carry out the following responsibilities: remain informed of all changes/updated in guidance/law at the federal and state levels to implement an timely Title IX program to the campus community; manage Title IX investigations; manage informal resolution processes; manage intake reports and provide supportive measures; maintain impeccable internal records of reports received, investigations conducted, and informal resolutions undertaken in both Maxient and Microsoft 360 OneDrive. The Title IX Specialist will also manage the annual online faculty and staff sexual harassment prevention training; conduct educational training workshops with students and employees across the university; assist with the editing of the handbooks and marketing materials; collaborate annually with stakeholders across the campus to develop and implement Title IX marketing campaigns; assist with the completion of the annual Clery, ISPHVE, and state mandated sexual misconduct student survey reports. Manage all activities/reports in the Maxient and Microsoft 365. Communications This position requires a person with strong communication skills to communicate clearly verbally and in writing, using effective interpersonal skills to understand complicated Title IX policies and regulations. The person will work directly with the Title IX Coordinator to interpret policy and draft internal and external documents and marketing material. This person will possess active listening skills and accurate note-taking ability as well as strong editing skills for use when editing office resources documents, policy manuals, marketing material, and letter-writing campaigns to make the language clear, accurate, and student-friendly whenever possible. Customer Service This position requires effective interpersonal skills, including the ability to demonstrate empathy and use a trauma-informed approach when addressing sexual misconduct. It also requires someone who possesses the ability to engage and build trust with students, campus partners, and community organizations on an ongoing basis, making sure to use language that encourages collaboration. Key Responsibilities - Develop, coordinate, deliver, document, and manage annual campus wide and targeted Title IX training for students and employees, ensuring compliance with applicable state and federal laws. Use varied training methods and maintain open communication with campus partners, participants, and volunteer investigators. - Lead Title IX events, campaigns, and presentations throughout the year, including Sexual Assault Awareness Month and Domestic Violence Awareness Month. Seek opportunities to collaborate annually with campus stakeholders in developing these programs. - Conduct and manage informal resolutions for eligible Title IX reports, meeting with both parties and assisting them in reaching mutually agreed resolutions. - Conduct and manage Title IX investigations, including fact finding, interviews, review of inculpatory and exculpatory evidence, credibility assessments, case status updates, and report writing. Manage case records in Maxient and Microsoft 365. - Receive and process reports of Title IX sexual harassment and provide supportive measures to Illinois Tech community members. - Assist with updates to handbooks and marketing materials and support Public Safety and General Counsel in completing annual Clery and ISPHVE reports and state mandated sexual misconduct student survey reports. Stay informed of current Title IX law through webinars, local workshops, and ongoing training. Education & Experience - Bachelor’s degree in a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. - Some experience working in higher education or a field related to the position (sexual assault, domestic violence, law, etc.). - Some familiarity with Title IX law and the Illinois Preventing Sexual Violence in Higher Education Act. - Must have the ability to leverage technical resources and build their own technical abilities in the execution of work. - Working knowledge of local resources in the Chicagoland area available to support the campus community is preferred. Knowledge & Skills - Familiarity with Title IX regulations and applicable State of Illinois sexual harassment laws. - Some experience with investigations, complaint handling, and resolution processes is preferred. - Proficiency in Microsoft 365 applications. - General familiarity with Maxient and Banner systems is preferred. Supervision & Budget Authority This position does not currently have direct supervisory responsibilities or budgetary authority. Physical Environment and Requirements - Works primarily in a standard office setting, performing administrative, programmatic, and computer-based tasks for the majority of the workday. - May occasionally attend meetings, events, or perform work-related duties at other locations throughout the University campus, with or without reasonable accommodation. - May occasionally lift and transport materials, such as boxes, supplies, or event items, weighing up to 15 pounds, with or without reasonable accommodation. - Regularly performs repetitive motions, including typing and other computer-related tasks, throughout the workday. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary EEO Statement Illinois Institute of Technology is an EEO/AA/Title VI/Title IX/Section 504/ADA/ADEA employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, inclusion, and diversity. It is committed to fostering an inclusive environment and actively seeks applications from individuals of all backgrounds and identities, regardless of race, color, sex, marital status, religion, national origin, disability, age, unfavorable discharge from the military, status as a protected veteran, sexual orientation, including gender identity and expression, order of protection status, and/or genetic information. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=19ee2990-a5f3-868d-5ca0-797b663d0cf5": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Enrollment Marketing",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Enrollment Marketing - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings Assistant Director of Enrollment Marketing Department: Marketing and Communications Location: Chicago, IL START YOUR APPLICATION Assistant Director of Enrollment Marketing Position Details Compensation: $65,000–$75,000 yearly, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Position Type/Schedule: Full-time Work Location: Illinois Institute of Technology, Chicago, Illinois Work Authorization: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States, both presently and for the duration of employment with the university. Position Summary The Assistant Director of Enrollment Marketing supports the development, execution, and optimization of data-driven enrollment marketing strategies that advance undergraduate and graduate enrollment goals. This position manages recruitment communications, campaign execution, CRM-based marketing initiatives, analytics reporting, and project management while collaborating closely with Enrollment Management, Marketing and Communications, campus partners, and external vendors. The Assistant Director plays an important role in developing and executing prospective student communication strategies across multiple channels and uses data and analytics to evaluate campaign effectiveness, improve engagement, and support the university's enrollment objectives. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Execute integrated enrollment marketing campaigns across email, web, digital advertising, social media, print, and SMS channels. Manage prospective student communication plans and recruitment journeys within CRM platforms such as Slate. Collaborate with Enrollment Management teams to support recruitment events, campus visits, counselor engagement, application campaigns, and other enrollment initiatives. Develop, schedule, and deploy enrollment communications while ensuring consistency with university brand standards and applicable accessibility requirements. Monitor campaign performance and prepare regular reports on key performance indicators, including inquiry generation, conversion rates, engagement metrics, and enrollment outcomes. Assist with lead-generation initiatives, list acquisitions, and partnerships with college search and planning organizations. Coordinate content development with Marketing and Communications, including landing pages, emails, digital advertisements, video, print collateral, and other recruitment materials. Manage project timelines, workflows, vendor relationships, and deliverables to ensure projects are completed accurately and on schedule. Support enrollment marketing budget tracking and return-on-investment analysis. Train and support staff and campus partners on enrollment marketing tools, communications, processes, and best practices. Develop and maintain documentation of enrollment marketing processes, workflows, and standards. Perform other duties as assigned in support of Enrollment Management and university objectives. Qualifications Bachelor's degree required. Minimum of two years of relevant professional marketing experience. Experience developing or executing multi-channel marketing or communications campaigns. Experience working with digital communications, email marketing, web content, or related marketing platforms. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects, deadlines, and stakeholders simultaneously. Ability to analyze campaign data and translate results into actionable recommendations. Strong written, verbal, organizational, and interpersonal communication skills. Preferred Competencies Experience working in higher education, enrollment management, admissions, student recruitment, or a related environment. Experience using a CRM platform, preferably Slate. Knowledge of enrollment marketing strategies and prospective student communication journeys. Familiarity with email marketing, SMS communications, digital advertising, social media, and web-based recruitment strategies. Experience with marketing analytics, performance reporting, conversion tracking, and ROI analysis. Strong project management skills with the ability to coordinate projects involving multiple departments and external partners. Demonstrated attention to detail and commitment to maintaining brand consistency and accessibility standards. Ability to work collaboratively with diverse stakeholders and effectively train or support campus partners. Ability to use data to identify opportunities, evaluate effectiveness, and continuously improve enrollment marketing initiatives. Supervision & Budget Authority May supervise coordinators, student employees, interns, or external contractors and provide project leadership for enrollment marketing initiatives. Supports budget tracking, vendor management, and ROI analysis for enrollment marketing activities. Budget authority, if applicable, is exercised in accordance with university policies and departmental approval processes. Physical Qualifications The position primarily operates in a professional office environment and routinely requires the use of a computer and other standard office equipment. The employee must be able to communicate effectively with colleagues, students, prospective students, vendors, and other stakeholders and perform the essential functions of the position with or without reasonable accommodation. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary EEO Statement Illinois Institute of Technology is an EEO/AA/Title VI/Title IX/Section 504/ADA/ADEA employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, inclusion, and diversity. It is committed to fostering an inclusive environment and actively seeks applications from individuals of all backgrounds and identities, regardless of race, color, sex, marital status, religion, national origin, disability, age, unfavorable discharge from the military, status as a protected veteran, sexual orientation, including gender identity and expression, order of protection status, and/or genetic information. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=be41e16a-867a-a026-0b27-c453707ecf16": {
      "title": "Senior Research Associate",
      "description": "Senior ResearchAssociate - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings Senior Research Associate Department: College of Tech Futures Location: Chicago, IL START YOUR APPLICATION Senior Research Associate Position Details Compensation: $70,000–$75,000 yearly, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Position Type/Schedule: Full-time Work Location: Illinois Institute of Technology, Chicago, Illinois Work Authorization: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States, both presently and for the duration of employment with the university. Summary The Built Environment Research Group (BERG) in the School of Engineering, Applied Science, and Health at Illinois Institute of Technology seeks a Postdoctoral Research Associate to support an interdisciplinary project developing and evaluating improvised building protection strategies for mitigating indoor exposure to outdoor aerosol hazards. The strategies must utilize common household items to devise systems that maintain positive indoor pressure through filtered outdoor air supply, as well as recirculating filtration to reduce exposure once particles enter a building. The successful candidate will integrate controlled-chamber experiments, field measurements, and physics-based modeling to determine how filter, fan, duct, building, and weather conditions affect air infiltration, particle penetration, energy use, comfort, and the reliability of protective operation. Key Responsibilities Key responsibilities entail: Plan and conduct large-chamber experiments to evaluate filter, fan, duct, and improvised connection configurations across airflow rates and pressure differentials. Measure and analyze indoor and outdoor fine and ultrafine particle concentrations, building pressure differences, airflow and air change rates, weather and thermal conditions, and electrical power use. Design and execute short- and long-term field studies in test homes and residences, including equipment installation, quality assurance, maintenance, and data retrieval. Estimate and interpret air change rates, particle penetration and infiltration factors, and indoor removal rates under baseline and positive pressurization conditions. Develop and validate single- and multizone airflow models using CONTAM or comparable tools, and conduct parametric analyses across building types, climates, weather conditions, and system configurations. Maintain organized data, code, experimental records, protocols, and quality control documentation to support reproducible research. Prepare peer-reviewed manuscripts, technical reports, conference presentations, sponsor updates, and public-facing guidance in text, visual, and video formats. Coordinate research activities with principal investigators and collaborators and mentor graduate and undergraduate researchers. Communications The postdoctoral researcher will maintain regular communication with the principal investigators through written updates and online and in-person meetings. The researcher will collaborate with students, participate in sponsor meetings, and clearly communicate research methods, findings, limitations, and progress to both technical and non-technical audiences. Education & Experience Required: A completed PhD, awarded by the appointment start date, in architectural engineering, civil engineering, mechanical engineering, environmental engineering, building science, aerosol science, or a closely related field. Research experience in at least one of the following areas: building airflow and infiltration, indoor air quality, aerosol measurement, HVAC filtration, building energy systems, or building performance modeling. Evidence of scientific productivity through peer-reviewed publications, conference papers, or comparable scholarly work. Demonstrated experience designing experiments, analyzing multivariable time-series data, and documenting research methods and results. Preferred Experience conducting chamber experiments or field studies in buildings. Experience with aerosol instrumentation, pressure and airflow measurements, tracer gas methods, or environmental monitoring systems. Experience with CONTAM or other airflow and building performance simulation tools. Experience coordinating research tasks, mentoring students, and collaborating with interdisciplinary teams or external sponsors. Knowledge & Skills Strong understanding of building airflow, pressure driven infiltration, ventilation, filtration, particle transport, and indoor mass balance principles. Ability to select, calibrate, deploy, troubleshoot, and maintain research instrumentation and data acquisition systems. Proficiency in data analysis and visualization using Python or comparable scientific software. Ability to develop, calibrate, and evaluate physics-based models and compare model predictions with measured data. Strong scientific writing, oral presentation, project organization, and collaborative problem-solving skills. Ability to work independently while managing multiple experimental, modeling, and dissemination activities. Certifications & Licenses No professional license is required. The selected candidate must complete applicable laboratory and field safety training before conducting project activities. Physical Environments The position combines office, laboratory, and field work. The researcher must be able to work on-site in the BERG laboratory and at field-study locations; transport, install, and maintain portable monitoring equipment; work around fans, filters, ducts, and data-acquisition systems; and enter residential and other building environments while following site-specific safety and occupant-protection procedures. Some local travel and work outside standard office hours may be required to support time-sensitive experiments or field measurements. Work environments include a normal office, shared workspace, laboratory, and residential or other field-study locations. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary EEO Statement Illinois Institute of Technology is an EEO/AA/Title VI/Title IX/Section 504/ADA/ADEA employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, inclusion, and diversity. It is committed to fostering an inclusive environment and actively seeks applications from individuals of all backgrounds and identities, regardless of race, color, sex, marital status, religion, national origin, disability, age, unfavorable discharge from the military, status as a protected veteran, sexual orientation, including gender identity and expression, order of protection status, and/or genetic information. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=e10788ff-dc5e-136a-f43b-089a593b78d7": {
      "title": "Arboretum Program Manager",
      "description": "Arboretum Program Manager - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings Arboretum Program Manager Department: Main Campus Physical Operations Location: Chicago, IL START YOUR APPLICATION Arboretum Program Manager Position Details Compensation: $90,000 - $95,000, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Position Type/Schedule: This is a full-time, exempt position with a regular Monday through Friday schedule. Occasional evening or weekend work may be required to support Arboretum programs, campus events, seasonal activities, or urgent tree and landscape needs. Work Location: Illinois Tech, 10 West 35 th Street, Chicago, IL 60616. Work Authorization: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States, both presently and for the duration of employment with the university. Position Summary The Arboretum Program Manager provides leadership, stewardship, and program management for the Alphawood Arboretum at Illinois Institute of Technology: Illinois Tech, a certified Level I arboretum located on the University’s historic campus in Chicago’s Bronzeville neighborhood. The position is responsible for advancing and maintaining a high-quality and diverse portfolio of trees, prairie plantings, and other herbaceous landscapes in an urban educational environment. Key areas of responsibility include arboretum stewardship, tree care and maintenance, landscape planning, project management, campus and community programming, and collaboration with academic, community, and industry partners. The Arboretum Program Manager works to ensure a safe, welcoming, sustainable, and aesthetically engaging outdoor environment for students, faculty, staff, tenants, visitors, and the surrounding community. The position reports to the Associate Vice President for Facilities and collaborates with University departments and external partners in support of the Arboretum’s educational, environmental, and community objectives. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities - Provide overall leadership and stewardship for the Alphawood Arboretum and support its continued development as a University and community resource. - Oversee tree care, condition assessment, maintenance, preservation, and safety activities for the University’s tree portfolio. - Develop and implement proactive tree and landscape management practices consistent with professional arboriculture, environmental, and safety standards. - Guide the continued expansion and diversification of the Arboretum’s tree and plant portfolio, including consideration of biodiversity, sustainability, campus history, landscape architecture, and long-term environmental conditions. - Grow the arboretum to reach Level II Accreditation. - Oversee the development and care of prairie plantings and other herbaceous landscapes associated with the Arboretum. - Plan and manage Arboretum and landscape projects, including project scope, vendor and contractor coordination, schedules, documentation, implementation, and preparation and coordination of materials supporting external funding opportunities for Arboretum programs and projects. - Maintain accurate tree, landscape, project, and program records using appropriate technology and information systems. - Develop educational programs, events, interpretive materials, tree walks, signage, and other resources that increase awareness and engagement with the Arboretum. - Collaborate with Faculty, students, and academic departments to support educational activities, experiential learning, and other academic initiatives that make appropriate use of the campus landscape and Arboretum resources. - Develop and maintain collaborative relationships with community organizations, public gardens, professional associations, industry partners, and subject matter experts. - Communicate Arboretum information, tree data, campus landscape information, and program activities to internal and external audiences. - Incorporate safety, environmental stewardship, sustainability, and applicable regulatory requirements into Arboretum activities and projects. - Perform other related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications - High school diploma or GED. - Arborist skill training. - Experience with tree care, arboriculture, landscape management, or a closely related area. - Ability to identify tree and plant species in the field. - Knowledge of tree care practices, including tree condition and safety, pruning, preservation, bracing, removal, soil conditions, fertilization, and disease and pest management. - Ability to read and interpret landscape plans and apply them to tree, plant, and outdoor projects. - Strong organizational, project management, problem-solving, and communication skills. - Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with University colleagues, contractors, community partners, and subject matter experts. - ISA Certified Arborist credential or ability to obtain the credential within an established period following hire. - Valid driver’s license. Preferred Qualifications - Bachelor’s degree in Forestry, Arboriculture, Natural Resource Management, Horticulture, Landscape Management, or a related field. - Five or more years of related tree care, arboriculture, landscape, or program management experience. - Experience managing an arboretum, public garden, campus landscape, or similar outdoor environment. - Experience coordinating landscape or facilities projects involving contractors and external service providers. - Knowledge of geographic information systems, tree inventory or tracking systems, computer-aided design, or related technology. - Pesticide Commercial Applicator/Operator License. - Aerial lift, fall protection, forklift, or related safety certifications. Service Standards and Performance Expectations - Provides professional, responsive, and collaborative service to students, faculty, staff, tenants, visitors, community members, contractors, and external partners. - Proactively identifies tree, landscape, safety, maintenance, and program needs and coordinates appropriate solutions. - Maintains accurate and current records, project information, and program documentation. - Communicates clearly and effectively with internal and external stakeholders regarding Arboretum activities, projects, programs, and concerns. - Effectively manages multiple priorities, projects, and seasonal responsibilities while maintaining appropriate attention to safety, quality, and deadlines. - Builds and maintains productive relationships across the University and with community, industry, and professional partners. - Demonstrates sound judgment, accountability, environmental stewardship, and a commitment to maintaining a safe and welcoming campus environment. Supervision & Budget Authority - Provides supervision and work direction to assigned union, non-union, and student employees supporting Arboretum and landscape activities. - Coordinates work performed by contractors, vendors, and other service providers associated with Arboretum projects and operations. - Oversees the Arboretum program budget and related expenditures in accordance with University policies and established approval processes. Physical Qualifications - Work is performed in both office and outdoor environments. - Must be able to travel throughout campus and work outdoors in varying weather conditions. - Position may require bending, kneeling, climbing stairs or ladders, and accessing landscape and tree-care work areas. - May occasionally work at heights or around equipment used in tree and landscape maintenance. - Must be able to safely perform the physical activities necessary to inspect trees, landscapes, and project sites. - Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position, consistent with applicable law. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary EEO Statement Illinois Institute of Technology is an EEO/AA/Title VI/Title IX/Section 504/ADA/ADEA employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, inclusion, and diversity. It is committed to fostering an inclusive environment and actively seeks applications from individuals of all backgrounds and identities, regardless of race, color, sex, marital status, religion, national origin, disability, age, unfavorable discharge from the military, status as a protected veteran, sexual orientation, including gender identity and expression, order of protection status, and/or genetic information. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=443435d3-9dc7-b47a-cd82-e11bbfa0e7ae": {
      "title": "Mens Lacrosse Head coach",
      "description": "Mens Lacrosse Head coach - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings Men's Lacrosse Head coach Department: Athletics Department Location: Chicago, IL START YOUR APPLICATION The salary range for this role is $55,000-$60,000 and is commensurate with experience Successful candidate will be responsible for leadership, administration, and coaching of a college men’s Lacrosse team. Responsibilities will include recruiting quality student athletes, organizing and planning practices, implementing game strategies, scouting, coaching, scheduling, budgeting and planning team travel in compliance with university, the NAAC Conference, and NCAA rules and regulations. Strong recruiting, communication and organizational skills are all required and candidates must demonstrate a willingness to follow all policies in place by the university and athletic department. The position will have a second duty as assigned by the Director of athletics. The ideal candidate will have excellent verbal and written communication skills. Must project a positive professional image and be enthusiastically engaged in creating a positive experience for student-athletes. Experience recruiting highly academically qualified student athletes is a must. This position does not provide customer service to external customers and provides limited customer service to internal customers. Must be willing to work some nights and weekends Key Responsibilities Adhere to and enforce all policies and procedures of the University, Department of Athletics, as well as the rules and regulations of the NAAC Conference and NCAA. Recruit and retain highly qualified student athletes. Ensure compliance with NCAA guidelines for contacting and entertaining prospects. Work closely with admissions department to ensure selection of appropriate student athletes. Provide leadership and instruction in the personal and athletic development of student athletes, including counseling team members in academic, disciplinary and personal matters, when appropriate. Initiate and coordinate the selection, purchase, fitting and maintenance of team equipment, to include uniforms, athletic equipment and supplies. Schedule and conduct regular practice sessions as permitted by NCAA rules and regulations. Develop and implement strategies for motivating student athletes to perform at maximum levels as both individuals and a team. Arrange team travel, lodging and transportation arrangements within specified budget. Provide a complete travel itinerary to director of athletics prior to each overnight trip. Ensure that the team dresses appropriately when traveling. Assist with approved fundraising activities as requested. All team fundraising efforts must be approved by the Director of athletics after fund raising proposal form has been completed. Assist in attempts to increase interest in the sport and attendance at competitions. Work with The Director of Athletics in developing and articulating to student athletes the departmental and team rules regarding appearance, practice, class attendance, punctuality, dress code and general standards of behavior. Enforce policies and procedures outlined in student athlete handbook, team rules and apply appropriate disciplinary action. Ensure the safety of student athletes and coaching staff through careful monitoring of the condition of athletic equipment and facilities utilized by the designated sport. Submit requests for repair, maintenance and improvement of facilities to the Director for facilities and operations. Assure that sport camps related to the sport program adhere to all rules and regulations related to scheduling and NCAA procedures. Review and clearly understand all sections of department employee handbook. All department employees are accountable for following this document. Additional duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics. Supervises assistant coach(es) and one student employee. Maintain Budget Bachelors degree and two years of experience coaching Men's Lacrosse required. Preference will be given to applicants with experience at the NCAA Division III level. Preferred requirements master's degree, 3-5 years of experience of collegiate coaching experience preferred. The successful candidate will possess excellent interpersonal skills, and the ability to work independently with little direction or no supervision. Evening and weekend work is required. No additional licenses or certifications are required. May be required to stand for long periods and must be able to lift at least 25lbs. No exposure to unpleasant conditions. The position requires long periods of standing approximately 50% of the time as well as administration of office duties 50% of the time. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=8f9faa6c-219f-1dab-0af1-b5bdb6386a3d": {
      "title": "Legal Operations & Project Coordination Paralegal",
      "description": "Legal Operations & Project Coordination Paralegal  - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings Legal Operations & Project Coordination (Paralegal) Department: General Counsel Location: Chicago, IL START YOUR APPLICATION Legal Operations & Project Coordination (Paralegal) Pay Range: $70,000– $75,000 per year Compensation Statement: The pay range listed reflects the anticipated base compensation for this role. Actual compensation will be determined based on skills, experience, education, and internal equity. Position Summary The University’s Office of General Counsel is responsible for providing legal advice and representation to the University, and to faculty and staff acting in their roles as representatives of the University. The successful candidate will be an organized, detail-oriented professional who can independently manage multiple priorities, coordinate complex projects, maintain confidential information, and work collaboratively with attorneys and University stakeholders. The Office of General Counsel is a small, collaborative team that supports the University’s academic, research, business, and governance activities across a wide range of legal matters. The work is varied and often fast-paced, with priorities that evolve as new legal issues arise. This position is ideal for a highly organized professional who enjoys coordinating complex work, improving processes, solving problems, and working collaboratively with attorneys and colleagues across the University. While many assignments follow established procedures, the position also provides opportunities to develop new skills, recommend improvements, and contribute to the continued effectiveness of the Office of General Counsel. Essential Duties and Responsibilities This position will work closely with the attorneys and the Assistant to the Vice President and General Counsel to support the legal, operational, and administrative responsibilities of the Office of General Counsel. Legal Operations & Project Coordination Work closely with the Office of General Counsel legal team to develop and improve office policies, procedures, and best practices for addressing legal and operational matters affecting the University. Coordinate and manage multiple legal and administrative matters simultaneously, ensuring deadlines, documentation, and deliverables are effectively tracked and completed. Coordinate and maintain compliance-related processes involving faculty, staff, and trustees, including tracking and maintaining required questionnaires, disclosures, and related records. Assist with the coordination of committees chaired by members of the Office of General Counsel. Perform other duties as assigned by the General Counsel. Contracts & Document Management Prepare and customize attorney-approved template agreements and related documents, including non-disclosure agreements, liability waivers and releases, and independent contractor service agreements. Update and maintain office databases for contracts, patents, international agreements, insurance, and other legal records and related information. File and maintain applicable state and municipal business licenses and permits. Assist in the maintenance and renewal of insurance policies. Litigation & Regulatory Support Conduct factual and legal research under attorney direction and supervision, and assist with the preparation, organization, and filing of court, government agency, and other legal documents, as needed. Support litigation and litigation-related activities, including coordinating responses to subpoenas, discovery requests, and other requests for records, as well as organizing related documentation. Coordinate the processing and tracking of wage liens, deductions, garnishments, and bankruptcy matters in collaboration with appropriate University offices. Governance Support Assist with Board of Trustees matters, including preparation of meeting materials, resolutions, officer’s certificates, committee materials, and related governance documentation. Administrative Support Provide general office administrative support. Such other duties as may be assigned by the General Counsel. Qualifications Three (3) years of progressively responsible professional experience supporting legal operations, project coordination, business operations, or related functions. Highly proficient in Microsoft Office (particularly Word and Excel), Adobe Acrobat, and database or document management systems. Strong organizational, project management, and time management skills. Excellent attention to detail. Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, and research skills, including the ability to communicate professionally and effectively with individuals at all levels of the University. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Paralegal certificate or comparable experience supporting legal operations. Prior experience in a legal environment is valuable, but not required. The Office of General Counsel is committed to helping the successful candidate develop familiarity with the University’s legal processes and subject areas. Notary Public certification. If not already a notary, eligibility to obtain such certification within 60 days of hire. Preferred Competencies Project Coordination Organization & Prioritization Communication & Relationship Building Legal & Administrative Operations Process Improvement Confidentiality & Professional Judgment Document & Records Management Problem Solving & Adaptability The normal hours for this position are 8:30 a.m. to 5:00 p.m., Monday through Friday. Applicants should submit a cover letter, current résumé, and a list of three references. Applications are considered confidential. References will not be contacted without prior notice to applicants. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=951f2625-9539-a573-3638-e4764762d3d1": {
      "title": "Director of Development",
      "description": "Director of Development - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings Director of Development Department: Advancement Location: Chicago, IL START YOUR APPLICATION The salary range for this role is $110,000-$135,000 and is commensurate with experience Position Summary The Director of Development is a frontline fundraiser responsible for identifying, qualifying, cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding major gift prospects capable of commitments of $100,000+. Directors manage a portfolio of prospects and support the university’s fundraising priorities across all academic units. Directors are assigned based on institutional priorities and will have primary fundraising responsibility for one or more academic units. Key Responsibilities 1) Major Gift Fundraising & Portfolio Management – 75% Manage a portfolio of major gift prospects (approximately 125), with capacity of $100,000+. Conduct approximately 100 donor visits per year, including at least 20 formal solicitations (may include blended or planned gifts). Qualify prospective donors through discovery to assess philanthropic interest, capacity, and alignment with university priorities. Develop individualized cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship strategies aligned with academic unit priorities. Achieve annual revenue goals aligned with experience and unit priorities (generally ~$1M–$3M). Maintain strong stewardship practices and solicit annual leadership gifts from assigned prospects. 2) Prospect Strategy, Research, & Analytics – 10% Partner with Managing Director and Prospect Research & Management (PRM) for portfolio optimization and pipeline development. Participate in regular portfolio reviews with the Managing Director and PRM. Prepare proposals, gift agreements, and donor correspondence in collaboration with Donor Relations and Gift Administration. Ensure timely and accurate documentation of all prospect activity in Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge NXT; adhere to stage movement and data integrity standards. Prepare briefing materials for meetings involving deans, faculty, or university leadership. Participate in Advancement meetings, prospect strategy reviews, and professional development trainings. 3) Academic Partnerships – 15% Serve as key liaison for one or more academic units; align fundraising strategies with dean-defined priorities and program needs. Develop deep knowledge of university and unit priorities. Partner with faculty and program leaders and understand student success initiatives, to align donor interests with institutional needs. Represent Advancement at donor and university events as assigned. Contribute to special projects and cross-unit initiatives that advance institutional and campaign fundraising goals. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Minimum of 5 years of fundraising (or closely related) experience with direct donor engagement and solicitation. Demonstrated success closing major gifts. Preferred Qualifications Advanced degree. 7+ years of frontline major gift experience. Experience with STEM and/or professional school donors. Strong communication and organizational skills. Experience with Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge NXT. Work Environment & Conditions Periodic out-of-state travel. Occasional evening or weekend work. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=dd59eccf-ec40-7108-8d1f-a0bc4dcfd997": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Development",
      "description": "Associate Director of Development - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings Associate Director of Development Department: Advancement Location: Chicago, IL START YOUR APPLICATION Pay Range : $80,000– $110,000 per year. The pay range listed reflects the anticipated base compensation for this role. Actual compensation will be determined based on skills, experience, education, and internal equity. Position Summary The Associate Director of Development is a frontline fundraiser responsible for identifying, qualifying, cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding major gift prospects capable of commitments of $100,000+. Associate Directors manage a portfolio of prospects and support the university’s fundraising priorities across all academic units. Associate Directors are assigned based on institutional priorities and will have primary fundraising responsibility for one or more academic units. Key Responsibilities 1) Major Gift Fundraising & Portfolio Management Manage a portfolio of major gift prospects (approximately 125), with capacity of $100,000+. Conduct approximately 100 donor visits per year, including at least 20 formal solicitations (may include blended or planned gifts). Qualify prospective donors through discovery to assess philanthropic interest, capacity, and alignment with university priorities. Develop individualized cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship strategies aligned with academic unit priorities. Achieve annual revenue goals aligned with experience and unit priorities (generally ~$1M). Maintain strong stewardship practices and solicit annual leadership gifts from assigned prospects. 2) Prospect Strategy, Research, & Analytics Partner with Managing Director and Prospect Research & Management (PRM) for portfolio optimization and pipeline development. Participate in regular portfolio reviews with the Managing Director and PRM. Prepare proposals, gift agreements, and donor correspondence in collaboration with Donor Relations and Gift Administration. Ensure timely and accurate documentation of all prospect activity in Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge NXT; adhere to stage movement and data integrity standards. Prepare briefing materials for meetings involving deans, faculty, or university leadership. Participate in Advancement meetings, prospect strategy reviews, and professional development trainings. 3) Academic Partnerships Serve as key liaison for one or more academic units; align fundraising strategies with dean-defined priorities and program needs. Develop deep knowledge of university and unit priorities. Partner with faculty and program leaders and understand student success initiatives, to align donor interests with institutional needs. Represent Advancement at donor and university events as assigned. Contribute to special projects and cross-unit initiatives that advance institutional and campaign fundraising goals. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Minimum of 3 years of fundraising (or closely related) experience with direct donor engagement and solicitation. Preferred Qualifications Advanced degree. 3-5 years of frontline major gift experience. Demonstrated success closing major gifts. Experience with STEM and/or professional school donors. Strong communication and organizational skills. Experience with Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge NXT. Work Environment & Conditions Periodic out-of-state travel. Occasional evening or weekend work. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=c344a992-0623-2740-386a-9d4c172beb6e": {
      "title": "Sr Director of Enrollment Operations",
      "description": "Sr Director of Enrollment Operations - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings Sr. Director of Enrollment Operations Department: Enrollment Services Location: Chicago, IL START YOUR APPLICATION Sr. Director of Enrollment Operations Pay Range: $100,000– $112,000 per year The pay range listed reflects the anticipated base compensation for this role. Actual compensation will be determined based on skills, experience, education, and internal equity. The Senior Director of Enrollment Operations is responsible for leading the operational strategy and execution of enrollment services across undergraduate, graduate, and international student populations. This role oversees the core infrastructure, technology systems, and processing operations that support the full enrollment lifecycle—from prospect to matriculation. The Senior Director will drive process improvements, manage cross-functional teams, and ensure data-driven decision-making to meet institutional enrollment goals. Qualifications Education: Master’s degree in higher education administration, business administration, or a related field. Experience: Minimum of 8+ years of progressive leadership experience in admissions or enrollment operations Demonstrated success in managing teams and improving enrollment-related business processes. Proficiency in CRM systems (e.g. Slate Technolotions), student information systems, and data management tools. Skills & Competencies: Strong strategic planning, leadership, and organizational abilities. Exceptional interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to inspire and lead diverse teams. Proficiency in enrollment analytics, market research, and forecasting. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities Enrollment Leadership & Strategy Serve as a senior leader in the Enrollment Management division, developing and executing an operational roadmap aligned with institutional goals. Supervise and mentor a multi-functional team, including admissions operations, CRM administration, application processing, and transfer credit evaluation. Act as the primary liaison between Enrollment Operations and institutional stakeholders, including academic units, student services, and IT. Operational Management Lead the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of standard operating procedures for admissions processing, data entry, and communications workflows. Oversee centralized operations across domestic and international applicant pipelines, ensuring compliance with institutional and federal guidelines. Ensure efficient processing of application materials, transcripts, test scores, and transfer credit evaluations. Technology & Systems Oversee the administration and optimization of the institution’s CRM (e.g., Slate Technolutions) Partner with campus partners to maintain data integrity, develop reporting tools, and support strategic enrollment analysis. Identify and implement automation and integration opportunities to improve processing speed and accuracy. Partnership Development and Stakeholder Engagement Ensure enrollment practices are compliant with institutional policies, FERPA, and accreditation standards. Oversee the preparation and delivery of regular reports and dashboards to senior leadership, tracking application volume, processing benchmarks, and conversion rates. Financial Measures Oversight of the Enrollment Operations budgets. Supervision Supervises & leads several teams, including undergraduate & graduate operations teams, CRM administration team, and transfer articulation team. Miscellaneous Some evening and weekend hours are required. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=7284c9ab-e90f-683f-e341-067badbfe306": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Assistant",
      "description": "Clinical Research Assistant - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings Clinical Research Assistant Department: Institute of Food Safety and Health Location: Bedford Park, IL START YOUR APPLICATION Clinical Research Assistant Pay Range : $50,000– $52,000per year The pay range listed reflects the anticipated base compensation for this role. Actual compensation will be determined based on skills, experience, education, and internal equity. Position Summary Assists with various aspects of human clinical trials with supervision. Aspects of clinical trials include recruiting, screening, enrollment, scheduling subject visits, data entry, quality control, anthropometic measurements, study food preparation. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Assists with coordination of clinical trials: Recruiting, screening, enrollment, scheduling subject visits, data entry, quality control, anthropometic measurements, study food preparation. Lab (kitchen lab and bio-labs) responsibilities will include sample/specimen preparation and processing, prepare food/meal per protocol and standard operating procedures. Food record analyses. Follows procedures to clean and sterilize lab (kitchen lab and bio-labs) equipment; assists in setting up, adjusting, operating and maintaining equipment and instruments according to procedures Follows established safety regulations and procedures. Performs routine maintenance as needed. Records data on trial-specified forms. Enters data into specified databases. Completes control checks on data after entry. Assists in supply inventory, maintains logs/journals. Qualifications Requires B.S. degree in Nutrition, Dietetics, or related field. Internship experience preferred. Requires analytical skills and attention to detail in conducting experiments. Requires basic nutrition and food knowledge. Requires basic knowledge in anthropometrics. Ability to multitask on projects and demonstrate good results orientation through a pro-active and team based approach. Preferred Competencies Communicates basic data and facts in a clear and concise manner to Supervisor in both verbal and written communications. Demonstrates good listening skills. Internal communications are routine and frequent. Communicates with line supervisor and project leader to determine immediate needs and deliverables. Performs basic internal communications referencing established timelines and metrics. Physical Environment and Requirements Works extensively in a clinical lab environment where there are strong safety procedures protective equipment requirements (wears lab coat, gloves, et)c, and works with various specimens and chemicals <1% May lift up to 10 lbs, 10% of time and performs extensive keyboarding (15%) and pipetting up to 10% of the time. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=2be330ef-23f3-9646-db29-c747d0f271a0": {
      "title": "Associate Vice President for Enrollment Management",
      "description": "Associate Vice President for Enrollment Management - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings Associate Vice President for Enrollment Management Department: Enrollment Services Location: Chicago, IL START YOUR APPLICATION The salary range for this position is $150,000–$200,000, with final compensation determined based on the selected candidate’s experience, skills, and overall qualifications. This broader range is intentional, allowing us to remain competitive and flexible in attracting top talent across varying levels of expertise within the market. Summary: The Associate Vice President for Enrollment Management (AVP) is a senior leader responsible for the strategic direction, execution, and continuous optimization of undergraduate and graduate enrollment efforts. Reporting to the Vice President for Enrollment Management & Student Affairs, the AVP leads a comprehensive enrollment enterprise that includes undergraduate and graduate admissions, recruitment marketing, enrollment communications, events and a robust portfolio of pre-college and pipeline programs. This role oversees the full enrollment lifecycle, including undergraduate and graduate admissions, recruitment marketing, enrollment communications, events, and a robust portfolio of pre-college and pipeline programs. The AVP will align enrollment initiatives with institutional priorities, market dynamics, and student demand, ensuring a cohesive and high-performing enrollment operation. A key priority for this role is the development and expansion of pre-college initiatives as a primary driver of long-term enrollment growth, student access, and institutional visibility. The AVP is accountable for building a sustainable pipeline of future students through innovative K–12 partnerships, summer programs, and pathway experiences that align with the university’s academic strengths. The AVP is accountable for achieving institutional enrollment goals by designing and implementing innovative, data-driven recruitment and yield strategies that strengthen the university’s market position, academic profile, and student diversity. This role ensures a seamless and high-quality prospective student experience from inquiry through matriculation. Working in close collaboration with the Associate Vice President for Student Financial Services and senior leadership in International Affairs, the AVP aligns recruitment, pricing, and global engagement strategies to drive enrollment outcomes across domestic and international markets. This role ensures seamless and high-quality prospective student experience from early pipeline engagement through matriculation. Qualifications Required Skills and Competencies Master’s degree in higher education, business administration, public administration, or a related field. Minimum of 10 years of progressive leadership experience in enrollment management, admissions, or related areas. Demonstrated success in developing and executing complex enrollment strategies with measurable outcomes. Experience managing multiple functional areas (e.g., admissions, marketing, recruitment operations). Demonstrated success in building and scaling enrollment pipelines, including pre-college or outreach programs. Strong analytical skills with experience leveraging data, CRM systems, and enrollment technologies to drive results. Experience leading cross-functional teams and complex enrollment operations. Proven ability to lead and develop high-performing teams in a dynamic environment. Excellent communication leadership, and stakeholder management skills. Strong analytical and strategic planning skills. Preferred Qualifications Experience in private, STEM-focused, or research-intensive university. Experience developing or managing pre-college, dual enrollment, or pathway programs. Familiarity with Slate CRM, Ellucian Banner, or similar systems. Experience with graduate and international enrollment strategies. Knowledge of financial aid leveraging and tuition revenue optimization. Experience managing external vendors, marketing agencies, or recruitment partners. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities: Strategic Enrollment Leadership Serve as a key architect of the university’s comprehensive enrollment strategy, integrating pre-college pipeline development with undergraduate and graduate enrollment goals with institutional priorities and long-term financial sustainability. Develop multi-year enrollment plans, including market segmentation, program positioning, and growth strategies across domestic and international populations. Leverage predictive analytics, CRM data, and market intelligence to guide decision-making and optimize funnel performance (inquiry – application – admit – enroll), including pre-college participation, conversion rates, and long-term enrollment yield. Establish and monitor KPIs related to application volume, admit rates, yield, net tuition revenue, and student quality indicators. Pre-College Programs and Pipeline Development (Elevated Priority) Provide executive leadership for a comprehensive portfolio of pre-college programs, including summer academies, dual enrollment, dual credit, certificate programs, and K–12 partnerships. Position pre-college as both a strategic enrollment pipeline and a potential revenue-generating enterprise, aligned with institutional growth goals. Design and scale innovative programming that introduces prospective students to high-demand academic areas, particularly in STEM and emerging disciplines. Build and sustain partnerships with high schools, school districts, community organizations, and corporate partners to expand access and strengthen brand presence. Develop clear pathways from pre-college participation to undergraduate enrollment, including early identification, engagement, and conversion strategies. Implement robust assessment models to track conversion, student success, and ROI of pre-college initiatives. Ensure alignment between pre-college offerings and institutional priorities related to access, diversity, and student readiness. Admissions and Enrollment Management Provide executive oversight for Undergraduate and Graduate Admissions, ensuring consistent, equitable, and efficient application review and decision processes. Lead the development and implementation of recruitment strategies across first-year, transfer, graduate, and online populations. Ensure alignment between admissions criteria and institutional goals for academic quality, access, and diversity. Partner with academic leadership to support new program launches and enrollment growth in high-demand disciplines. Recruitment Marketing and Communications Oversee integrated recruitment marketing strategies including digital marketing, content development, brand positioning, and enrollment communications. Oversee integrated marketing strategies that connect pre-college outreach with broader recruitment campaigns. Collaborate with Marketing & Communications to develop data-driven campaigns that increase awareness, engagement, and conversion. Ensure effective use of CRM platforms (e.g., Slate) to deliver personalized, timely, and segmented communications across the recruitment funnel. Continuously evaluate ROI on marketing channels and adjust strategies to maximize impact. Events and Yield Strategy Lead the strategy and execution of on-campus and virtual recruitment events, including open houses, admitted student programs, and counselor engagement initiatives. Lead a comprehensive events strategy that includes pre-college programming, summer experiences, and yield-focused engagement initiatives. Design high-impact yield strategies that enhance student engagement and drive enrollment decisions. Ensure a cohesive and differentiated campus visit experience that reflects the institution’s value proposition. Collaboration with Financial Aid and International Affairs Partner closely with the AVP for Student Financial Services to align recruitment strategies with financial aid leveraging, scholarship policies, and net revenue goals. Collaborate with International Affairs leadership to strengthen international recruitment pipelines, partnership, and student support services. Ensure coordinated strategies across domestic and international markets to optimize enrollment mix and global diversity. Collaborate with International Affairs to explore pre-college and pathway programs for international students. Operational Excellence and Team Leadership Provide leadership and development for a high-performing, diverse team across admissions, marketing, events and pre-college programming. Foster a culture of accountability, innovation, collaboration, and continuous improvement. Ensure efficient operational processes, including application processing, communications workflows, and event execution. Oversee budget planning and resource allocation across enrollment functions, including investment and revenue models for pre-college programs. Campus Partnership and Representation Serve as a key liaison to academic colleges, Student Affairs, Registrar, and other campus partners to support enrollment and retention initiatives. Represent Enrollment Management on institutional committees and strategic initiatives. Contribute to institutional planning related to student success, retention, and the overall student experience. Financial Measures Oversee a budget of up to $5 to 8 million in Operations. Supervision This role will be supervisory in nature, overseeing at least 5 to 7 direct reports and 30 to 50+ in-direct reports and teams. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=b141135e-b789-2236-efc6-aaef401feb9d": {
      "title": "International Student Advisor",
      "description": "International Student Advisor  - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings International Student Advisor Department: Office of Global Services Location: Chicago, IL START YOUR APPLICATION The salary range for this role is $48,000-$52,000 and is commensurate with experience Illinois Institute of Technology’s Office of Global Services seeks an International Student Advisor who will primarily serve the diverse international student population at Illinois Tech. The advisor will also be expected to provide support to international scholars as needed. The selected candidate focuses on providing accurate, compassionate, individualized advising and processing to incoming and present international students and Illinois Tech departments while ensuring institutional compliance with federal regulations governing Illinois Tech sponsored statuses. General Description: The International Student Advisor provides support and assistance to the Office of Global Services. This position is responsible for advising international students on F-1 and J-1 immigration regulations and cultural adjustment and will serve as a (DSO) Designated School Official and (ARO) Alternate Responsible Officer for the F-1 and J-1 programs in compliance with Federal regulations. This position will assist with SEVIS operations, document and application processing and support general office needs. This position will help coordinate and lead educational programs for students, faculty, and staff. Advising staff regularly interprets regulations and university policy and draws conclusions after various possibilities are considered. Advisors recommend and implement policy based on analysis of immigration regulations, government guidance and best practices. The incumbent must be a U.S. Citizen or Permanent Resident as required by federal regulations for certification as a (DSO) Designated School Official and and (ARO) Alternate Responsible Officer. Communications: 1) In coordination with Management team- Respond to University or U.S. Government requests for data validation. 2) Review regular OGS’ targeted electronic communications with international students and scholars, and University divisions about programs and events. 3) Develop and deliver presentations to clientele in public forums. 4) Maintain standard protocols in working with confidential documents and sensitive data. Customer Service: Provides customer service to internal and external customers (all listed above in Communication). Positive relationships and customer service are extremely important when dealing with the IIT community, especially international students. A survey is sent to all international students every other year to evaluate the office’s services. Informal feedback is given from other IIT departments, faculty, and staff. Key Responsibilities 1: 55% Advising services- a. Advise F-1 students and/or J1 students/scholars on immigration regulations, cultural adjustment, academic and English language difficulties, financial concerns and general orientation to life in the U.S. b. Participate in bi-weekly advisor meetings c. Provide consistent and correct information d. Serve as On Call advisor on rotating basis e. Keep abreast of current issues affecting student population f. Oversee & Process student documents including but not limited to: Program extension, CPT, OPT, OPT Extension, Transfer Out, Academic Training, Workflow g. Keep abreast of changes in visa regulations; Key Responsibilities 2: Regulatory Compliance 40% Act as a Designated School Official (DSO) and/or Alternate Responsible Officer (ARO). b. Monitor international student and/or scholar compliance with government regulations. c. Evaluate university policy and ensure compliance with immigration regulations. Remain current with SEVIS-related and regulatory updates pertaining to international students and scholars to ensure institutional compliance. e. Assist management team in compliance reporting including SEVIS Registration, address and employment updates and maintenance of status. Key Responsibilities 3: Other 5% Other duties as assigned by Supervisor, Division, or University. Education and Experience: Bachelor’s degree in related field required. Two years (2) or more, relevant work experience in a higher education environment or combination of education and experience. Experience with international student and exchange scholar populations and regulations, including understanding of SEVIS, F, and J visa requirements. Very strong preference for experience with Terra Dotta and Banner. Expertise in use of MS Office applications, especially, Word, Excel, and Outlook. Experience in the use of university students and personnel information systems. Familiarity with FERPA regulations; Strong interpersonal, collaborative, organizational, analytical, and oral/written communication skills. Ability to multitask, work independently, and manage complex projects. US Citizenship or Permanent Residence required to access SEVIS Database. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=fd559f94-a7ab-b8d4-e03a-b1123b60eafa": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Accounts Receivable",
      "description": "Assistant Director Accounts Receivable - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings Assistant Director, Accounts Receivable Department: Student Financial Services Location: Chicago, IL START YOUR APPLICATION The salary range for this role is $60,000-$65,000 and is commensurate with experience. GENERAL DESCRIPTION Illinois Tech Student Financial Services strives to educate, empower, and support students with an understanding of financial options and resources in an approachable environment. Reporting to the Director of Student Accounting, the Assistant Director for Accounts Receivable is a key leader in the Student Accounting Office and a member of the enrollment management team, providing leadership on all aspects of the student account receivable lifecycle including accounts receivable setup and account resolution. This role will support the Director in execution of new partnerships, student billing, third-party receivables, and 1098T generation within the Office of Student Accounting and will provide support for reporting and audit requirements. This role will supervise the student account analyst and ensure a high-quality experience across all key operations and services. COMMUNICATIONS Excellent communication skills required when working with university staff, outside vendors and current and prospective students. Broad knowledge of university functions and depth of student accounting function necessary to cultivate relationships with students and across campus. CUSTOMER SERVICE Excellent customer service required when working with university staff, outside vendors and current and prospective students. Broad knowledge of university functions and depth of financial aid requirements necessary to cultivate relationships with students and across campus. The ability to maintain student confidentiality is essential in this position. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Services Responsible for generating all student billing statements each enrollment period to support student payment and university cash operations. This includes fee assessments within the Banner and StarRez systems along with providing support to the Director in the setup and maintenance of the rate tables, new charges, and ad hoc fees. Coordinate bill distribution with Student Accounting leadership to support service demands and enrollment timelines each enrollment cycle. Assess late penalty charges for delinquent accounts and oversee support for student needs outside of the standard billing timelines. Apply past due holds in the system in alignment with the enrollment periods to ensure university policy on enrollment with a past due balance is tightly monitored. Oversee process to ensure students using third-party support are processed in a timely manner each term. Operations Provide support for all university partnership billing setup and reporting. Liaise with key enrollment partners to ensure billing structure supports enrollment goals including but not limited to Residence Life, Student Health and Wellness, and all admission units. Create and manage the university billing calendar in conjunction with key stakeholders across the university to ensure billing timelines meet the enrollment and cash flow needs of the university. Oversee collections with third-party partner, Recovery Select, for all outstanding balances each term. Ensure support provided to partner to meet university enrollment goals for future terms. Prove reporting for all activities and outcomes. Monitor daily reports to ensure data needs align with desired billing generation and reporting. Work closely with the Student Accounting and Financial Aid leadership to ensure all processes and systems are working to meet the operational needs. Compliance Oversee the generation and distribution of 1098Ts as required annually. Provide support to the director and any partner offices for annual financial audits. Support enrollment leadership in reporting requirements and needs to ensure accounts receivable operations meet all compliance needs and university strategic goals. Leadership Supervise the Student Account Analyst in third-party billing process including by not limited to student assignments, invoicing, and reporting. Provide escalation support for all service needs with a solution mindset to support the student experience and positive team culture. Provide regular training to the student accounting staff on all service, processing, and operational needs in collaboration with student accounting and financial aid leadership. Contribute to the implementation and assist in the development, modification of and writing Student Accounting policies and procedures for the office. Key member of the Student Accounting leadership team providing guidance and making recommendations to the AVP in determining and address inefficiencies. Represent the Director and/or designee in their absence or as requested. Other duties and special projects as assigned. Events : This role will work at several events each aid year to assist students and families in understanding the billing process and options for payment. Some nights and weekends are required for university events. Other duties as assigned. SUPERVISION & BUDGET AUTHORITY Supervisor at least one staff member to support accounts receivable needs. EDUCATION & EXPERIENCE Bachelor’s required. Minimum of 5-7 years of progressive experience in bursar, accounts receivable, or third-party billing services. KNOWLEDGE AND SKILLS Experience in bill generation and third-party collections. Knowledge of federal student/student aid regulations and guidelines Proficiency using Microsoft Excel for data analysis and visualization Preferred knowledge of Ellucian Banner or College software; other system knowledge beneficial as well. Exercises great attention to detail utilizing analytical and problem-solving skills. Demonstrate the ability to adapt in a high pace environment Must keep abreast of changing guidelines for cash management and student collections. Must be able to manage multiple projects and coordinate with collaborators simultaneously. Demonstrated ability and experience to handle complex and sensitive issues. Strong written and verbal communications with proven ability to maintain collaborative relationships with internal and external constituents in order to provide support for the office and the students it serves required. Demonstrated ability to work in a team-based environment. Excellent commitment to diversity and to service the needs of a diverse population Demonstrated ability to efficiently and effectively solve problems and initiate and implement projects independently Interacts effectively with peers and superiors to address and resolve issue Influences management by supplying key data that assists in decision making CERTIFICATIONS & LICENSES: N/A Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary PHYSICAL ENVIRONMENT & REQURIEMENTS Office environment; must be able to sit at computer for long periods of time. START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=b5a4e220-0d80-24a2-3090-801903d10f6e": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Student Services & Veteran School Certifying Official",
      "description": "Assistant Director Student Services & Veteran School Certifying Official - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings Assistant Director, Student Services & Veteran School Certifying Official Department: Student Financial Services Location: Chicago, IL START YOUR APPLICATION The salary range for this role is $55,000-$60,000 and is commensurate with experience. GENERAL DESCRIPTION Illinois Tech Student Financial Services strives to educate, empower, and support students with an understanding of Financial options and resources in an approachable environment. Reporting to the Director of Financial Aid Services, the Assistant Director for Student Services & Veteran School Certifying Official is a key leader of the Financial Aid Office and a member of the enrollment management team, providing leadership on the student experience, particularly as it relates to veteran student needs, along with support for all aspects of the student experience related to Financial aid and veteran benefit processing. This role will support the Director in providing direct student services and triage support in the Office of Financial Aid. This role will serve as the VA School Certifying Official and manage the veteran student experience from benefit processing, student advising, recruitment support, and veteran related compliance. Communications Excellent communication skills required when working with university staff, outside vendors and current and prospective students, including in-person and virtual advising, presentations, email, and phone outreach. Customer Service Excellent customer service required when working with university staff, outside vendors and current and prospective students. Broad knowledge of university functions and depth of Financial aid requirements necessary to cultivate relationships with students and across campus. The ability to maintain student confidentiality is essential in this position. Education & Experience Bachelor’s required. Minimum of 5 years of progressive experience in veterans affairs, financial aid, admissions, or enrollment services. Military Veteran or knowledge of military experience, benefits, and transcripts is beneficial KNOWLEDGE & SKILLS Exercises great attention to detail utilizing analytical and problem-solving skills. Demonstrate the ability to adapt in a high pace environment Must keep abreast of changes with Federal Student Aid and Veterans/ Military benefits programs. Must be able to manage multiple projects and coordinate with collaborators simultaneously. Demonstrated ability and experience to handle complex and sensitive issues. Strong written and verbal communications with proven ability to maintain collaborative relationships with internal and external constituents in order to provide support for the office and the students it serves required Demonstrated ability to work in a team-based environment Excellent commitment to diversity and to service the needs of a diverse population Demonstrated ability to efficiently and effectively solve problems and initiate and implement projects independently Works well in translating financial aid requirements into operational activities supporting overall enrollment efforts Influences management by supplying key data that assists in decision making Physical Environment and Requirements Office environment; must be able to sit at computer for long periods of time. List any certifications or licenses that are either required or helpful in performing the job, designating whether required or preferred. N/A Key Responsibility Services Counsel students (in person, virtually, over phone, and email) on all aspects of the financial aid process, including FAFSA completion, cost of attendance, awarding of federal funds, loan borrowing and management, financial hardship situations, etc. Serve as member of counseling team to support student appointments (in-person & virtual) and walk-in needs. Assist in the direction of student inquiries to other staff as needed and provide leadership to the counseling staff for escalation needs Meet with students in a co-terminal program to ensure aid receipt based on enrollment is understood so students can plan course schedule accordingly In support of the Director of Financial Aid Services, provide escalation assistance for all service needs with a solution mindset to support the student experience and positive team culture Percentage Of Time25 Key Responsibility Operations Process ROTC funds for eligible students; coordinate with each branch to ensure timely process each term and assist students in understanding impact on overall aid offer Oversee financial aid processing needs for key populations such as part-time scholarship requests, reinstatements, and scholar programs Assist with reconciliation and discrepancies with Student Accounting for veteran and special populations going through third-party billing Assist with completion of financial aid processes including but not limited to verification, c-flags, private loan processing, etc. Process financial aid hardship appeals in accordance with federal professional judgement guidelines Process satisfactory academic progress (SAP) appeals to review students in continued eligibility for federal aid Percentage Of Time20 Key Responsibility Veterans Adhere to all VA principles of excellence to provide high quality services and support to veteran students Certify enrollment and benefits each term for benefits eligible students, including allowable tuition and fees; monitoring any changes in enrollment or aid to ensure accuracy and ensure VA benefits are processed as last payer with all other applicable aid by working closely with the Offices of the Registrar and Student Accounting Ensure cost transparency based on VA guidelines with the maintenance of the shopping sheet in conjunction with the Senior Financial Aid Director Provide timely support for all veteran student data for annual financial audits and periodic veteran compliance surveys Supply data validation for all veteran student reporting requirements, including internal and external requirements such as IPEDS and USNews surveys Monitor student’s standards of progress and report ineligible students to the VA accordingly Maintain proper record retention in accordance with the VA guidelines Counsel students processing veteran benefits on financial, enrollment, and any other needs that may arise to support overall student success for this population Liaise needs internally to ensure veteran students have holistic support throughout academic career Working collaboratively with admissions, marketing, financial aid, and academic affairs units for the purpose of recruiting military students, including attending events to support enrollment and retention Remain current regarding state, federal, and university regulations and policies related to veteran’s benefits and federal compliance Support the development of and serve on a Veteran’s Services task force with key stakeholders from enrollment, academics, and student affairs to develop and support a robust veteran experience at Illinois Tech Collaborate the delivery of special veterans’ related programming (ex: Veterans Day, Memorial Day, and veterans support groups) with key campus stakeholders Conducts training for faculty and staff on matters related to veteran student needs Percentage Of Time35 Key Responsibility Compliance Liaise between student and government agencies to address inquiries and resolve issues with federal aid or veteran benefits eligibility and/or processing Provide input on any financial aid or veteran compliance related policies and procedures to ensure continued organizational and student eligibility for funds Ensure all required university documentation for processing all military benefits is kept current and monitored by key university leadership stakeholders Percentage Of Time10 Key Responsibility Leadership Serve on the financial literacy committee and assist the Director of Financial Aid Services in providing programming, tools, and support for student literacy and cost planning needs Provide support to all financial aid staff to resolve financial aid discrepancies and resolve issues to ensure integrity in aid administration Provide regular training to the financial aid staff on all service, processing, and operational needs in collaboration with the Senior Director and Director of Financial Aid Services Contribute to the implementation of Financial Aid and university policies and procedures for the office Other duties and special projects as assigned Percentage Of Time5 Key Responsibility Events This role will work at several events each aid year to assist students and families in understanding the financial aid process, their individual aid offer, veteran benefit options, and enrollment next steps. Some nights and weekends are required for university events. Percentage Of Time5 Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=bdc6c097-b09e-f932-b820-a58310582dc2": {
      "title": "Intramurals and Recreation Coordinator",
      "description": "Intramurals and Recreation Coordinator - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings Intramurals and Recreation Coordinator Department: Athletics Department Location: Chicago, IL START YOUR APPLICATION The salary range for this role is $50,000-$55,000 and is commensurate with experience GENERAL DESCRIPTION: Under the supervision of the Director of Athletics, the Intramurals and Recreation Coordinator manages and operates the intramural and recreation program in accordance with the purposes and policies of the Keating Sports Center and Illinois Tech Athletic Department. The Intramurals and Recreation Coordinator is responsible for the supervision of staff, fiscal operations, program development, marketing/public relations, participant retention, and customer service related to the intramural & recreation programs at Illinois Tech. COMMUNICATIONS: Written, verbal, and electronic communication are essential for this position. A large portion of this position will be interaction with internal staff and external constituents. CUSTOMER SERVICE:Customer service is crucial for this position. Student interaction and understanding of their needs is paramount for the success of the intramural activities and club events. This would require calibration with the Campus of Student Life. External relationships are a significant area, and relationships will be cultivated via the community affairs office and meetings with specific groups. Special Schedule Requirements: Hours of work will typically be from 8:30AM-5:00PM or 1:00PM – 9:00 PM, and/or as required by the Athletic Director. Some evening and weekend hours necessary. SUPERVISION & BUDGET AUTHORITY: This position will supervise at least 20-40 student workers each semester. Number of students supervised is dependent upon number of events offered. Budget authority for $40K EDUCATION & EXPERIENCE: Bachelor’s degree and 2-3 years of professional experience in campus recreation including customer service, recreational programming, sports leagues, human relations required, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Master’s degree preferred. KNOWLEDGE & SKILLS: Understanding of youth and community sports programming. Must have the ability to work with and/or collaborate with community organizations such as the YMCA, park district, and boys and girls’ clubs. Demonstrated skills in sport league coordination. Demonstrated coordination of special events. Demonstrate supervisory skills; demonstrate excellent communication skills, both written and oral; demonstrate ability to create and develop new programs; demonstrate ability to market programs and manage budgets; and demonstrate working knowledge of ongoing intramural programming. Physical Environment and Requirements: The position will be generally an office environment but participation in an indoor recreation setting and occasionally outdoor environment will be necessary. Ability to occasionally lift equipment up to 50lbs required. Significant time standing up, walking across campus, and climbing stairs meeting with campus departments essential (50%). Certifications and Licenses: YMCA Program Director certification desired, upon hiring will be required within one year. Membership with NIRSA (National Intramural-Recreation Sports Association) upon hiring will be required; preferably an active role in the organization. Key Responsibilities Hires, trains, supervises and evaluates staff, including student employees, related to the intramural & recreation programs. Develops a preventive maintenance program for all equipment related to the intramural & recreational programming area. Collaborates with co-workers, organizations and agencies in the community that help to reach the objectives of the Keating Sports Center and Illinois Tech Athletic Department. Monitor the use, storage, and distribution of intramural inventory. Percentage Of Time: 30 Provides a variety of sports related activities to the Illinois Tech community including sports leagues, tournaments, fitness classes, etc. Working closely with Campus Life and Student Orgs providing space for their usage, and coordinating events for our general student body, faculty, and staff. Oversees coordination and scheduling of fitness classes, athletic clubs, intramural leagues and tournaments. With existing budget, hire and schedule qualified and skilled instructors for classes. Percentage Of Time: 30 Develops a comprehensive marketing plan for all intramural leagues, special events, and collaborative sports programs, including athletic clubs. Aids in student, faculty, and staff retention and recruitment. Communicate effectively with team captains, officials, and Intramural Supervisors. Attend all Orientation (SOAR) and Admissions Events (Discover Days, etc.) to promote intramural and recreational programs. Percentage Of Time:10 Develops written policies and procedures as needed, including risk management procedures, to conduct the intramural and recreation program in the best and safest manner for the Keating Sports Center. Develop and coordinate an officials’ training and evaluation program. Percentage Of Time: 10 Develops and manages the approved income and expense budgets of intramural and recreation program. Attends all necessary meetings. Assumes responsibility for supervision of IIT Athletic facilities as they relate to the programs and as needed. Percentage Of Time: 20 Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=53eda2f6-94fe-7a83-dec8-1cd354bf25d8": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Student Experience and Events",
      "description": "Associate Director of Student Experience and Events - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings Associate Director of Student Experience and Events Department: Student Affairs Location: Chicago, IL START YOUR APPLICATION Associate Director of Student Experience and Events Position Details Compensation: $52,000 - $60,000, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Position Type/Schedule: Full-Time, exempt. Monday–Friday, 8:30 a.m.–5:00 p.m. This position is fully on-site; remote work is not available. Evening and weekend work is required for pre-scheduled major admission events, student programs, and other recruitment and engagement initiatives. These scheduling needs are generally planned in advance, and employees will receive advance notice whenever practicable. Occasional travel within the Chicagoland area, elsewhere in Illinois, or other domestic locations may be required. Work Location: I llinois Tech, 10 West 35th Street, Chicago, IL 60616 Work Authorization: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States, both presently and for the duration of employment with the university. Summary The Associate Director of Student Experience and Events leads the planning, coordination, execution, and assessment of Illinois Tech’s undergraduate and graduate admission events across in-person and virtual formats. Reporting to the Director of Admission Events, Student Experience and Visit Operations, the Associate Director serves as the primary operational lead for the admission event portfolio and translates enrollment priorities into high-quality recruitment and yield experiences for prospective and admitted students and their families. The Associate Director manages events from planning through post-event assessment, including campus partner coordination, logistics, communications, staffing, budget administration, and day of execution. The position works closely with admission and recruitment teams, Enrollment Marketing, academic leadership, faculty, staff, student employees, and other campus partners Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities Admission Event Strategy and Operations - Lead planning and execution of undergraduate and graduate admission events across in-person and virtual formats. - Develop event plans, timelines, staffing assignments, operational procedures, contingency plans, and measures of success. - Manage event logistics, including registration, space planning, guest services, technology, dining, transportation, signage, supplies, and related operational needs. - Serve as a visible event leader and primary operational resource for addressing issues affecting schedule, staffing, facilities, technology, and guest experience. Campus Partnerships and Team Coordination - Coordinate participation of academic units, faculty, staff, students, and campus partners in admission events and recruitment programs. - Partner with Enrollment Marketing, Facilities, Public Safety, Dining, technology, space management, and other campus stakeholders to support successful event delivery. - Work closely with the Assistant Director and Visitors Center Operations Coordinator to coordinate student engagement, campus visit activity, staffing, and shared resources. - Provide functional leadership to professional Staff, student employees, University partners, and others assigned to admission events, establishing clear roles, expectations, and accountability. Post Event Assessment and Resource Management - Conduct post event reviews using attendance, participant feedback, satisfaction, conversion, yield, and other relevant measures to evaluate overall effectiveness. - Prepare event recaps and identify key outcomes, lessons learned, and recommendations to strengthen future programs and operations. - Reconcile event expenditures, purchasing, vendor commitments, and other resources in partnership with the Director. - Evaluate vendor performance and resource use to identify efficiencies and inform future planning. Required Qualifications - Bachelor’s degree in higher education, business administration, communications, marketing, hospitality, event management, student affairs, or a related field. - Four or more years of progressively responsible experience in higher education, admissions, event management, student engagement, hospitality, or a related area. - Demonstrated experience planning and managing complex, high visibility events or programs involving multiple stakeholders and competing priorities. - An equivalent combination of education and relevant professional experience may be considered. Preferred Qualifications - Master’s degree in higher education, business administration, communications, marketing, hospitality, event management, student affairs, or a related field preferred. - Supervisory, team leadership, or significant project leadership experience. - Experience supporting recruitment, enrollment, prospective or admitted student engagement, or campus visit programs in a higher education environment. - Experience with Slate or comparable CRM, event management, scheduling, or reporting systems. - Experience with Square POS preferred. Service Standards and Performance Expectations - Demonstrated leadership and project management skills, including setting priorities, coordinating resources, assigning responsibilities, and maintaining accountability for results. - Ability to translate enrollment and event priorities into well coordinated programs, operational plans, and consistent service standards. - Strong judgment, problem solving, and decision making skills, with the ability to respond effectively in fast paced and highly visible event environments. - Strong communication and relationship management skills with the ability to collaborate effectively with University Leadership, faculty, Staff, students, vendors, and campus partners. - Ability to manage multiple complex priorities while maintaining organization, accuracy, operational readiness, and a high level of service. - Strong analytical skills with the ability to use event results, participant feedback, and relevant enrollment data to evaluate outcomes and support continuous improvement. Supervision - This position does not currently have direct professional Staff reports; however, supervisory responsibilities may be assigned in the future based on departmental needs. Physical Qualifications - Ability to effectively use standard office technology and equipment in a primarily in-person campus environment. - Ability to move throughout campus and stand or walk for extended periods during events. - Ability to occasionally lift, carry, and move event materials, supplies, signage, or equipment weighing up to 25 pounds. - Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position, consistent with applicable law. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; lifelidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by band long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university hoenefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary EEO Statement Illinois Institute of Technology is an EEO/AA/Title VI/Title IX/Section 504/ADA/ADEA employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, inclusion, and diversity. It is committed to fostering an inclusive environment and actively seeks applications from individuals of all backgrounds and identities, regardless of race, color, sex, marital status, religion, national origin, disability, age, unfavorable discharge from the military, status as a protected veteran, sexual orientation, including gender identity and expression, order of protection status, and/or genetic information. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=6bafadde-3139-f7fe-bfe1-bdfe97d17f06": {
      "title": "Director of Admission Events, Student Experience and Visit Operations",
      "description": "Director of Admission Events Student Experience and Visit Operations - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings Director of Admission Events, Student Experience and Visit Operations Department: Student Affairs Location: Chicago, IL START YOUR APPLICATION Director of Admission Events, Student Experience and Visit Operations Position Details Compensation: $70,000 - $75,000, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Position Type/Schedule: Full-Time, exempt. Monday–Friday, 8:30 a.m.–5:00 p.m. This position is fully on-site; remote work is not available. Evening and weekend work is required for pre-scheduled major admission events, student programs, and other recruitment and engagement initiatives. These scheduling needs are generally planned in advance, and employees will receive advance notice whenever practicable. Occasional travel within the Chicagoland area, elsewhere in Illinois, or other domestic locations may be required. Work Location: I llinois Tech, 10 West 35th Street, Chicago, IL 60616 Work Authorization: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States, both presently and for the duration of employment with the university. Summary The Director of Admission Events, Student Experience, and Visit Operations provides strategic leadership for Illinois Tech’s prospective and admitted student engagement programs, including undergraduate and graduate admission events, student engagement programs, campus visits, and Visitors Center operations. Reporting to the Associate Vice President of Enrollment Management, the Director establishes priorities, experience standards, resource allocation, and measures of success across these areas. The Director leads a team responsible for delivering coordinated, high-quality experiences for prospective and admitted students and their families. The position works closely with enrollment leadership, admission and recruitment teams, academic units, Enrollment Marketing, faculty, and other campus partners to support student engagement, conversion, yield, and institutional connection. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities Strategic Leadership and Team Management - Lead strategy and priorities for admission events, student engagement programs, campus visits, and Visitors Center operations in alignment with enrollment goals. - Supervise and develop the Associate Director, Assistant Director, and Visitors Center Operations Coordinator, establishing clear responsibilities, expectations, and accountability. - Oversee staffing, student employee programs, and operational coverage for major events, high volume visit periods, and engagement programs. - Evaluate program needs, resources, and opportunities for improvement and serve as the escalation point for complex operational issues. Campus Partnerships and Program Coordination - Build and maintain partnerships with academic units, Enrollment Marketing, Financial Aid, Student Affairs, Facilities, Public Safety, Dining, Event Services, and other campus partners. - Coordinate campus participation in admission events, visits, recruitment programs, and yield initiatives. - Partner with enrollment and recruitment leadership to ensure programs and experiences support undergraduate and graduate enrollment goals. - Promote consistent service standards, messaging, and institutional representation across student and family experiences. Assessment and Continuous Improvement - Establish measures of success and monitor participation, attendance, satisfaction, conversion, yield, and other relevant program data. - Partner with Enrollment Operations and other colleagues to support reporting and assessment using Slate and other systems. - Use program results and year over year trends to improve staffing, communication, resource allocation, and service delivery. - Present findings and recommendations to enrollment leadership and campus partners as appropriat e. Required Qualifications - Bachelor’s degree in higher education, business administration, communications, marketing, hospitality, event management, student affairs, or a related field. - Five or more years of progressively responsible experience in higher education, admissions, enrollment management, event leadership, student engagement, visitor experience, or a related area. - Three or more years of supervisory, team leadership, or significant organizational leadership experience. - An equivalent combination of education and relevant professional experience may be considered. Preferred Qualifications - Master’s degree in higher education, business administration, communications, marketing, hospitality, event management, student affairs, or a related field preferred. - Experience supporting prospective or admitted student engagement in a higher education environment. - Experience with Slate or comparable CRM, event management, scheduling, or reporting systems. - Experience with Square POS preferred. Service Standards and Performance Expectations - Demonstrated leadership and people management skills, including setting priorities, developing Staff, delegating effectively, and maintaining accountability for results. - Ability to translate enrollment priorities into coordinated strategies, programs, and service standards across multiple student facing functions. - Strong judgment, analytical ability, and decision-making skills, with demonstrated use of data and assessment to evaluate performance and guide improvements. - Executive level communication and relationship management skills with the ability to collaborate effectively with University Leadership, faculty, Staff, students, vendors, and campus partners. - Ability to lead complex, highly visible initiatives, manage competing priorities, and maintain consistent service, operational effectiveness, and institutional standards. - Strong organizational and problem-solving skills with the ability to anticipate needs, address challenges, and drive continuous improvement. Supervision - Directly supervises the Associate Director of Student Experience and Events, Assistant Director of Student Experience and Events, Visitors Center Operations Coordinator, and other positions as assigned. - Provides oversight through these positions for admission events, student engagement programs, campus visits, Visitors Center operations, and associated student employees. Physical Qualifications - Ability to effectively use standard office technology and equipment in a primarily in-person campus environment. - Ability to move throughout campus and stand or walk for extended periods during events. - Ability to occasionally lift, carry, and move event materials, supplies, signage, or equipment weighing up to 25 pounds. - Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position, consistent with applicable law. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary EEO Statement Illinois Institute of Technology is an EEO/AA/Title VI/Title IX/Section 504/ADA/ADEA employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, inclusion, and diversity. It is committed to fostering an inclusive environment and actively seeks applications from individuals of all backgrounds and identities, regardless of race, color, sex, marital status, religion, national origin, disability, age, unfavorable discharge from the military, status as a protected veteran, sexual orientation, including gender identity and expression, order of protection status, and/or genetic information. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=45dd1b81-81dc-5ec1-34b2-7743c0c40cd4": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Student Experience and Events",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Student Experience and Events - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings Assistant Director of Student Experience and Events Department: Student Affairs Location: Chicago, IL START YOUR APPLICATION Assistant Director of Student Experience and Events Position Details Compensation: $47,000 - $53,000, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Position Type/Schedule: Full-Time, exempt. Monday–Friday, 8:30 a.m.–5:00 p.m. This position is fully on-site; remote work is not available. Evening and weekend work is required for pre-scheduled major admission events, student programs, and other recruitment and engagement initiatives. These scheduling needs are generally planned in advance, and employees will receive advance notice whenever practicable. Occasional travel within the Chicagoland area, elsewhere in Illinois, or other domestic locations may be required. Work Location: I llinois Tech, 10 West 35th Street, Chicago, IL 60616 Work Authorization: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States, both presently and for the duration of employment with the university. Summary The Assistant Director of Student Experience and Events leads student powered recruitment and engagement initiatives that strengthen connections between prospective and admitted students and the Illinois Tech community. Reporting to the Director of Admission Events, Student Experience and Visit Operations, the Assistant Director provides primary professional leadership and oversight for the TeleHawk and SOAR (Student Orientation, Advising, and Registration) programs, as well as support to Hawk Ambassador and Graduate Student Assistant programs, and other student engagement programs, partnerships, and initiatives as assigned by Leadership. The role is responsible for student recruitment, selection, training, supervision, scheduling, development, performance management, and program assessment. The Assistant Director also plays an active role in undergraduate and graduate admission events, working closely with the Director, Associate Director, Visitors Center Operations Coordinator, admission and recruitment teams, and campus partners to integrate student leadership and authentic student engagement throughout recruitment, campus visit, event, and enrollment experiences. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities - Lead the TeleHawk and SOAR (Student Orientation, Advising, and Registration) programs, as well as support to Hawk Ambassador and Graduate Student Assistant programs, and other student engagement programs, partnerships, and initiatives as assigned by Leadership.including program goals, expectations, procedures, calendars, and operating standards. - Develop student leadership and employment experiences that promote accountability, professional development, engagement, and effective representation of Illinois Tech. - Maintain program resources, training materials, operating documentation, and other tools necessary for effective administration. - Identify opportunities to strengthen student to student engagement throughout the prospective and admitted student experience. Student Employee Recruitment, Training and Supervision - Lead recruitment, interviewing, selection, onboarding, and training of student employees for the TeleHawk and SOAR (Student Orientation, Advising, and Registration) programs. - Establish clear performance expectations and provide coaching, feedback, performance management, recognition, and professional development for student employees within these programs. - Develop staffing schedules and monitor attendance, availability, hours, coverage, and staffing needs across the TeleHawk and SOAR programs. - Share oversight of the Hawk Ambassador Program with the Visitors Center Operations Coordinator, coordinating student development, training, performance, operational needs, and daily campus visit activities. Admission Event Support and Program Assessment - Support the planning and execution of undergraduate, graduate, and virtual admission events under the leadership of the Associate Director. - Lead student employee staffing for major admission events, including assignments, expectations, training, and event day coverage. - Assess student engagement programs using participation, retention, performance, staffing, feedback, and other relevant measures and provide recommendations for improvement. - Support student employment administration, staffing resources, and related program expenditures in coordination with the Director and Associate Director. Required Qualifications - Bachelor’s degree in higher education, business administration, communications, marketing, hospitality, event management, student affairs, or a related field. - Two or more years of professional experience in higher education, admissions, student engagement, student employment, orientation, events, or a related area. - Demonstrated experience working with, advising, training, mentoring, or developing college students. - An equivalent combination of education and relevant professional experience may be considered. Preferred Qualifications - Master’s degree in higher education, business administration, communications, marketing, hospitality, event management, student affairs, or a related field preferred. - Experience coordinating or supervising student employees or student leadership programs. - Experience supporting recruitment, enrollment, campus visit, orientation, or large-scale event programs in a higher education environment. - Experience with Slate or comparable CRM, scheduling, student employment, or event management systems. Service Standards and Performance Expectations - Demonstrated ability to lead, coach, develop, and support student employees while maintaining clear expectations, accountability, and performance standards. - Strong organizational and project management skills with the ability to coordinate multiple student programs, schedules, and competing priorities. - Strong judgment and problem-solving skills, including the ability to address student employee performance, conduct, scheduling, and interpersonal concerns appropriately. Strong communication and relationship management skills with the ability to collaborate effectively with professional Staff, students, campus partners, and other stakeholders. - Ability to develop and facilitate effective training, professional development, and student leadership programming. - Strong service orientation with the ability to create welcoming, professional, and consistent experiences for prospective students and families. Supervision - Provides direct and/or programmatic supervision for TeleHawks, SOAR Leaders, and Hawk Ambassadors, as well as other student positions as assigned. Physical Qualifications - Ability to effectively use standard office technology and equipment in a primarily in-person campus environment. - Ability to move throughout campus and stand or walk for extended periods during events. - Ability to occasionally lift, carry, and move event materials, supplies, signage, or equipment weighing up to 25 pounds. - Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position, consistent with applicable law. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary EEO Statement Illinois Institute of Technology is an EEO/AA/Title VI/Title IX/Section 504/ADA/ADEA employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, inclusion, and diversity. It is committed to fostering an inclusive environment and actively seeks applications from individuals of all backgrounds and identities, regardless of race, color, sex, marital status, religion, national origin, disability, age, unfavorable discharge from the military, status as a protected veteran, sexual orientation, including gender identity and expression, order of protection status, and/or genetic information. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=7c519454-af20-82f1-d57c-40d8c431920d": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Student Success and Retention",
      "description": "Assistant Director Student Success and Retention - Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Career Opportunities with Illinois Institute of Technology A great place to work. Careers At Illinois Institute of Technology Share with friends or Subscribe! Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Subscribe to our RSS feeds to receive instant updates as new positions become available. Back To Openings Assistant Director, Student Success and Retention Department: Student Affairs Location: Chicago, IL START YOUR APPLICATION Assistant Director, Student Success and Retention Pay Range: $50,000 – $55,000 per year Compensation Statement: The pay range listed reflects the anticipated base compensation for this role. Actual compensation will be determined based on skills, experience, education, and internal equity. Position Summary The Office of Student Success is under the umbrella of the Student Affairs Division dedicated to promoting student achievement, well-being, and active participation in the campus community. This office works collaboratively with students, faculty, and staff to create programs, provide resources, and foster a supportive environment conducive to academic and personal growth. Under the direct supervision of the Director of Student Affairs, the Assistant Director of Student Success is a full-time professional staff member. The person in this role oversees the administration, leadership, and management of the programming, operations, and retention efforts for select scholarship cohorts such as Chicago Difference and Hope Scholars, and first-generation student success initiatives (i.e. peer mentor programs, commuter services, etc.). The person in this position will also lead their team in the development, coordination, and maintenance of a comprehensive peer mentorship program for first-generation students at Illinois Tech to ensure their success, engagement, and retention. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Recruit, supervise, train, and evaluate 10-15 student peer mentors who will work with Chicago Difference and Hope Chicago scholars. Partner with Undergraduate Admission and Elevate College Prep to build relationships with CPS partners and act as an advisor for outreach and strategic-enrollment initiatives. Duties may include representation at school visits, on campus recruitment events, and partner meetings. Throughout the year, collaborate with Elevate College Prep to build programming for CPS partners to create an enrollment pipeline for grades 9-12 through The Chicago Difference. In the spring, collaborate with Undergraduate Admission to select and onboard the upcoming fall cohort of Chicago Difference scholars. Connect current Chicago Difference Scholars with incoming scholars upon cohort selection in February. Provide leadership, administration, and create a sense of belonging for first generation students and scholarship cohorts such as the Chicago Difference and Hope Scholars. Serve as official representative for Hope Chicago program. Facilitate MOU. In partnership with the Office of Student Life, plan and facilitate monthly educational initiatives supporting student leadership development. Serve as an advocate for first generation students; lead community conversations about bias and community responses to bias as it relates to student concerns. Foster community building within the first-generation population and provide resources for students to connect to and from social support networks. Create and maintain meaningful partnerships and collaborations across the division, as well as with other academic and administrative on campus. Serve on university committees to establish and implement programs and services which enhance the retention and success of first-generation students. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required; Master's degree preferred in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Counseling, Educational Leadership, or related field. At least two years of relevant experience with a complex institution such as a university, school system, not-for-profit agency, or related is required. Supervision Direct supervision of 10-15 student peer mentors. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary START YOUR APPLICATION Visit Our Home Page © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
